{title: I Need Thee Every Hour}
{lyricist: Annie S. Hawks}
{lyricist: Robert Lowry}
{composer: Robert Lowry}
{year: 1872}
{key: G}
{meta: tune NEED}
{meta: variation The hymn, sung to NEED}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: note Hawks wrote the stanzas and Lowry added the refrain.}
{meta: tags prayer, dependence}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I [G]need Thee every [C]hour,
[G]Most gracious [D]Lord;
[G]No tender [G7]voice like [C]Thine
[G]Can [D]peace af[G]ford.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
I [D]need Thee, O I [G]need Thee;
[D]Every hour I [G]need Thee!
O [C]bless me [G]now, my [C]Savior,
I [G]come [D]to [G]Thee.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I [G]need Thee every [C]hour,
[G]Stay Thou near[D]by;
[G]Temptations [G7]lose their [C]power
[G]When [D]Thou art [G]nigh.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I [G]need Thee every [C]hour,
[G]In joy or [D]pain;
[G]Come quickly [G7]and a[C]bide,
[G]Or [D]life is [G]vain.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
I [G]need Thee every [C]hour;
[G]Teach me Thy [D]will;
[G]And Thy rich [G7]prom[C]ises
[G]In [D]me ful[G]fill.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
I [G]need Thee every [C]hour,
[G]Most Holy [D]One;
[G]O make me [G7]Thine in[C]deed,
[G]Thou [D]blessed [G]Son.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
